    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309-a1">

                <pb facs="0379" n="1113" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1113"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    190.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prince Lobanow to Mr.
                            Breckinridge.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                5 17, 1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    the note you kindly addressed to me, under date of November 17/29, concerning
                    the recognition in quality of citizens by the United States, on their return to
                    their country of origin, of Russian subjects having embraced American
                    nationality without the authorization of the Imperial Government.</p>
                <p>I have not failed to devote the most serious attention to the contents of said
                    note, and I hasten to inform you that this question will be the subject of a
                    careful examination on the part of the Imperial Government.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lobanow.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
